e polkadot race today for the rider that posts the quickest time up the CÃ´te de Larringes. Pogacar is the current leader in the mountains classification but Valentin Paret-Peintre (Soudal-Quick-Step) is wearing the jersey (skinsuit today) because the race leader canâ€™t wear both. The Frenchman will be emptying the tank up the climb, not worrying too much about his overall time, and hoping the GC leaders try to pace themselves a bit more evenly later on. Paret-Peintre has about 4km to go on the climb. One to keep an eye on.</p><p><strong>We are counting down</strong> to the GC leaders rolling off the start ramp, here are the scheduled start times for the top ten:</p><p>Jordan Jegat (TotalEnergies) at 15.57 BST (16.57 CEST)</p><p>Tom Pidcock (Pinarelloâ€“Q36.5) at 15.59 BST (16.59 CEST)</p><p>Lenny Martinez (Bahrain Victorious) at 16.01 BST (17.01 CEST)</p><p>Mattias Skjelmose (Lidl-Trek) at 16.03 BST (17.03 CEST)</p><p>Juan Ayuso (Lidl-Trek) at 16.05 BST (17.05 CEST)</p><p>Florian Lipowitz (Red Bull Boraâ€“Hansgrohe) at 16.07 BST (17.07 CEST)</p><p>Paul Seixas (Decathlon) at 16.09 BST (17.09 CEST)</p><p>Isaac Del Toro (UAE Emirates-XRG) at 16.11 BST (17.11 CEST)</p><p>Remco Evenepoel (Red Bull Boraâ€“Hansgrohe) at 16.13 BST (17.13 CEST)</p><p>Tadej Pogacar (UAE Emirates-XRG) at 16.15 BST (17.15 CEST)</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/sport/live/2026/jul/21/tour-de-france-2026-punishing-stage-16-time-trial-on-the-shores-of-lake-geneva-live">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KWpfYli3ehcZHuNrioOvOFdGmgy5HTNRUIjL3R9_DWAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;XCmjRdpRBVlDP9I0yQm6o0ZlNdAQcCyCn_fF8v_dLsgƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;uHd4jlDDp1zf4zk-LL9Z-xpItNUlJToGjFl_XPSOVBoƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;aPl0BawuZEP7hWspeOK8